  "text": "# Dinitrogen, N₂\n\nTwo nitrogens joined by a triple bond, solved by restricted Hartree–Fock in STO-3G: 10 orbitals, 7 occupied, E = −107.496 E_h.\n\nThe cloud is orbital 7 of 10, the HOMO: a σ orbital along the bond, bulging outward past each nucleus. Just below it, orbitals 5 and 6 are the degenerate π pair; 8 and 9, the LUMOs, are the empty π* pair.\n\nIn MO-REGISTRY, left-click the HOMO and one LUMO on the ORBITAL ladder and switch MO-REGISTRY ON: the density beats at their frozen-orbital gap Δε.\n\nUnder the chevron in MOLECULES, set KICK AXIS to Z — along the bond — then KICK and RUN: only the transitions polarised along the bond answer, and the spectrum Im α(ω) grows from them."
